 "notes": "The raw step (January-September 2026 against July-December 2025, each against the same week a year earlier) is +3.4 log points for ambulance travel and +7.6 for taxi time per mile. Placebo year (2024-W27 to 2025-W39, split 2025-W01): b = 0.68 (0.23 to 1.13), c = 0.008 (-0.027 to 0.044). Life-threatening only: b = 0.96, c = -0.019 (-0.051 to 0.012). The weekly slope (0.89) is above the hourly elasticity (0.63) of ems-traffic-hourly-elasticity; with 0.63 the taxi step predicts +4.8 points against the observed +3.4. This confirms that the 2025-to-2026 step in Manhattan is in proportion to the fall in taxi speed; it does not explain the larger 2019-2025 rise, which ems-traffic-share-2019-2026 attributes mostly to something other than traffic. Deviation from the plan: on 13 November the TLC file host refused downloads for about 30 minutes, so lib.taxi_hourly was changed after registration to read the cbd and north rows of data/derived/congestion/taxi_speed_*.csv for July 2023 to December 2025. Those rows use the same areas, the same trip filter and the same TLC files; the estimators were not changed. Months 2021-07 to 2023-06 and 2026-01 to 2026-09 were computed here.",
